srt-test-live 1.5.7 cannot send over a socket group: SrtTarget::ConfigurePre sets SRTO_SENDER on the group, which
libsrt refuses as an option of a link ("option is socket- or link-specific"), so srt-test-live -g ends before it
connects. SRTO_SENDER only matters to an HSv4 peer, and a group needs HSv5 on both sides, so a group skips it.
--- a/testing/testmedia.cpp
+++ b/testing/testmedia.cpp
@@ -2451,6 +2451,11 @@
     if (result == -1)
         return result;

+    // A group's links are HSv5 only, and libsrt refuses SRTO_SENDER on a
+    // group, as an option of a link.
+    if (sock & SRTGROUP_MASK)
+        return 0;
+
     int yes = 1;
     // This is for the HSv4 compatibility; if both parties are HSv5
     // (min. version 1.2.1), then this setting simply does nothing.
